`--no-lessons` drops the `## Lessons` section from the composed render, leaving the output a
lesson-free playbook would produce. The fixture is vault-attached and spreads its lessons across
both discovery roots — the global `{home_dir}/_lessons/` and the project `{vault}/_lessons/` — so
the flag is shown suppressing both.

Twin of `the-no-lessons-flag-removes-the-step-lesson-block.txtar`, same fixture tree.

-- fixtures/cwd/.booping --
project_name: probe
vault_path: ./vault
latest_migration: 9999
-- fixtures/home/Claude/_lessons/0002_step.md --
---
title: Step rule
targets: [fx-no-lessons/s1]
---

Step-scoped body.
-- fixtures/cwd/vault/_lessons/0001_alpha.md --
---
title: Alpha rule
targets: [fx-no-lessons]
---

Alpha body.
-- fixtures/cwd/vault/_playbooks/fx-no-lessons/playbook.md --
---
name: fx-no-lessons
title: No Lessons
summary: Lesson suppression on both surfaces.
---

Preamble.
-- fixtures/cwd/vault/_playbooks/fx-no-lessons/playbook.yaml --
graph:
  s1: []
-- fixtures/cwd/vault/_playbooks/fx-no-lessons/s1/prompt.md --
---
name: s1
summary: Only step.
detached: sonnet:medium
---

Step body.
-- cmd --
booping render-playbook fx-no-lessons
booping render-playbook fx-no-lessons --no-lessons
-- exit --
0
-- stdout --
